"Let $G$ be a graph. Write ${\\rm STAB}(G)$ for its stable set polytope and ${\\rm ASTAB}^*(G)$ for the polyhedral relaxation associated with joined a-perfect graphs. A graph is **${\\rm LS}_+$-perfect** when ${\\rm LS}_+(G)={\\rm STAB}(G)$, where ${\\rm LS}_+(G)$ is the Lovász–Schrijver positive semidefinite relaxation applied to ${\\rm ESTAB}(G)$.\n\n**${\\rm LS}_+$-perfect graph conjecture.** A graph $G$ is ${\\rm LS}_+$-perfect if and only if\n\n$$\n{\\rm STAB}(G)={\\rm ASTAB}^*(G).\n$$\n\nEquivalently, the conjecture asserts that ${\\rm LS}_+$-perfect graphs coincide with joined a-perfect graphs, with ${\\rm ASTAB}^*(G)$ serving as the corresponding polyhedral relaxation of ${\\rm STAB}(G)$."